  object PlusMemo1: TPlusMemo
    Left = 38
    Top = 89
    Width = 654
    Height = 490
    Cursor = crIBeam
    Alignment = taLeftJustify
    BorderStyle = bsNone
    HideSelection = False
    Lines.Strings = (
      #2#21'Welcome to Notepad Plus!'#21#2
      'by'
      #1#2'Electro-Concept Mauricie'#2#1
      'Web: http://www.ecmqc.com/'
      'email: ecm@ecmqc.com'
      ''
      
        #4'{This is the only time that this text will be displayed when st' +
        'arting this program.'#4
      
        #4'If you want to see it again in the future, click on "Display In' +
        'tro on Startup" under the File menu item.'#4'}'
      ''
      
        #1#2'Notepad Plus'#2#1' is a demo application for the '#1'TPlusMemo'#1' compo' +
        'nent and its accessories.  What'#39's in '#1'TPlusMemo'#1':'
      ''
      
        '  '#9#21#1'Native VCL'#1#21' enhanced memo component for Delphi 5 to Delphi' +
        ' XE, CBuilder 6 to XE.  Easily interchangeable with TMemo.  Supp' +
        'orts all of its features.  '#1'TDBPlusMemo'#1' is also available in th' +
        'e '#1'PlusMemo'#1' package.'
      ''
      
        '  '#9#21#1'Automatic syntax highlighting'#1#21': your keywords and sections' +
        ' are dynamically formatted to your liking.  Language highlighter' +
        's are also available.  To see it in action, use the "Syntax" rad' +
        'io group above.  Also look at the "Syntax" menu to define your o' +
        'wn keywords and sections, effective when you select "Custom" opt' +
        'ion in the syntax group.'
      ''
      
        '  '#9#21#1'Large text capability'#1#21', handles more than 100MB on modern ' +
        'system.'
      ''
      
        '  '#9#21#1'Selective text formatting'#1#21': parts of the text can be stati' +
        'cally turned to '#2'bold'#2', '#21'underline'#21', '#1'italic'#1', '#3'color highlight'#3 +
        ', '#4'alternate font'#4', or any '#4#3#21#1#2'mix of these attributes'#2#1#21#3#4'.  T' +
        'his information is saved with control codes embedded in the text' +
        '.  Text is formatted by the end user by selecting it and pressin' +
        'g Ctrl-B, Ctrl-I, Ctrl-U, Ctrl-H or Ctrl-F.  It can be formatted' +
        ' programmatically also.'
      ''
      
        '  '#9#21#1'Various useful enhancements'#1#21': multi level Undo-Redo, drag ' +
        'and drop editing, auto indenting, programmable line spacing, mar' +
        'gins, justification, vertical cursor navigation, saving in RTF f' +
        'ormat, clickable hot spots, printing support, ...'
      ''
      
        '  Concerning '#1'PlusMemo'#1' accessories, you already see two of them' +
        ' in action: the gutter at the left of this window is a "'#2#1'TPlusG' +
        'utter'#1#2'".  The Internet url highlighting that you see presently ' +
        '(ex: www.scientifique.com) comes from a"'#2#1'TURLHighlighter'#1#2'".  T' +
        'his demo uses also a "'#2#1'TPlusMemoPrinter'#1#2'", that you can launch' +
        ' by clicking on the printer or print preview button above.  You ' +
        'can also get collapsible sections by loading a .ini file, which ' +
        'is done through the use of "'#2#1'TpmCollapseHandler'#1#2'"   These, and' +
        ' other ones, are handy, easy to use companion components and ava' +
        'ilable for free from our web site.'
      ''
      
        'You can use Notepad Plus as you want.  You may find it an intere' +
        'sting replacement for Windows Notepad,  or as a simple code edit' +
        'or.  It has been written in Delphi and the source code is availa' +
        'ble on our web site, so you can extend it as you like.'
      ''
      'Enjoy!'
      ''
      #1#2'Electro-Concept Mauricie'#2#1
      'Web http://www.ecmqc.com/'
      'email: ecm@ecmqc.com'
      '')
    ScrollBars = ssBoth
    OnChange = PlusMemo1Change
    AltFont.Charset = DEFAULT_CHARSET
    AltFont.Color = clWindowText
    AltFont.Height = -13
    AltFont.Name = 'Times New Roman'
